From: AshesTom <258768419+AshesTom@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: set the system colours a visual style does not name to XP's defaults

Purpose: draw tooltips black on light yellow under the Windows XP style, as XP does.
XP behavior: uxtheme's loader starts from its default colours (loader.cpp
DefaultColors: InfoText 0 0 0, InfoBk 255 255 225, HotTracking 0 0 128,
...) and replaces those the style's [SysMetrics] names; it then sets all 31.
Luna names no tooltip colours in any of its styles.
Wine before: only the style's colours were set (and, in the XP session, the
hot-tracking one, patch 0160), so the scheme used before kept the others:
after the Eggplant scheme, tooltips had purple text on white under Luna.
Change: in the XP session, the colours a style does not name are XP's
defaults; 0160's hot-tracking colour is one of them.
Evidence: XP source at Source/XPSP1/NT/shell/themes/uxtheme/loader.cpp
(DefaultColors, InitThemeMetrics, SetSystemMetrics); luna.msstyles'
[SysMetrics] names no InfoText or InfoBk.
Scope: the XP session (WIN4WINE_SHELL=xp).
---
diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c b/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
@@ -831,18 +831,31 @@
 
 static void parse_apply_color (struct PARSECOLORSTATE* state)
 {
-    /* XP's styles name no hot-tracking colour except Luna's Silver: on XP the
-     * others keep the scheme's, HIVEDEF.INF's 0 0 128, the colour of links
-     * (SysLink); here the one of the style applied before would stay. */
-    if (win4wine_shell() == WIN4WINE_SHELL_XP && state->colorCount < ARRAY_SIZE(state->colorElements))
+    /* XP's uxtheme sets all the system colours of a style, those it does not
+     * name to its defaults (loader.cpp's DefaultColors): Luna names no tooltip
+     * colours (black on 255 255 225) and, but for Silver, no hot-tracking one
+     * (0 0 128, the colour of links). Here the colours of the scheme applied
+     * before would stay (Eggplant's purple tooltip text). */
+    static const COLORREF defaults[] =
     {
-        int i;
-        for (i = 0; i < state->colorCount; i++)
-            if (state->colorElements[i] == COLOR_HOTLIGHT) break;
-        if (i == state->colorCount)
+        RGB(212, 208, 200), RGB(58, 110, 165), RGB(10, 36, 106), RGB(128, 128, 128), RGB(212, 208, 200),
+        RGB(255, 255, 255), RGB(0, 0, 0), RGB(0, 0, 0), RGB(0, 0, 0), RGB(255, 255, 255),
+        RGB(212, 208, 200), RGB(212, 208, 200), RGB(128, 128, 128), RGB(10, 36, 106), RGB(255, 255, 255),
+        RGB(212, 208, 200), RGB(128, 128, 128), RGB(128, 128, 128), RGB(0, 0, 0), RGB(212, 208, 200),
+        RGB(255, 255, 255), RGB(64, 64, 64), RGB(212, 208, 200), RGB(0, 0, 0), RGB(255, 255, 225),
+        RGB(181, 181, 181), RGB(0, 0, 128), RGB(166, 202, 240), RGB(192, 192, 192), RGB(206, 211, 225),
+        RGB(244, 244, 240),
+    };
+    if (win4wine_shell() == WIN4WINE_SHELL_XP)
+    {
+        int color, i, count = state->colorCount;
+        for (color = 0; color < ARRAY_SIZE(defaults) && state->colorCount < ARRAY_SIZE(state->colorElements); color++)
         {
-            state->colorElements[state->colorCount] = COLOR_HOTLIGHT;
-            state->colorRgb[state->colorCount++] = RGB(0, 0, 128);
+            for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
+                if (state->colorElements[i] == color) break;
+            if (i < count) continue;
+            state->colorElements[state->colorCount] = color;
+            state->colorRgb[state->colorCount++] = defaults[color];
         }
     }
     if (state->colorCount > 0)
